[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pulls/997","id":4288680526,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSeuyxc7_oBJO","html_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pull/997","diff_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pull/997.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pull/997.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/issues/997","number":997,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix: complete the cover letter at the export boundary and repair the pipeline regressions","user":{"login":"saeedkolivand","id":51081940,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDgxOTQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51081940?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand","html_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## The bug\n\nThe staged pipeline's letter prompt (`pipeline/resume/prompts.rs`, `letter_system`) tells the model:\n\n> Do NOT write a contact header, a salutation line, or a signature block — **the application adds them at export time**.\n\nThe application never did. `parse_cover_letter` only ever *parsed* those parts out of a full letter. The résumé side of the identical promise **is** kept (`validate/mod.rs`, `ContactProfile::apply_to_header`), which is why résumés looked right and letters did not.\n\nIntroduced by `19a6de3e` (apply flow → staged pipeline), which deleted the one-shot TS path along with `extractMetadata`, the full-letter prompt, the market-conventions block and company research. Not by the agentic deletion in `93174a1c` — that prompt actually produced complete letters.\n\n### What a real German letter rendered as\n\n| Slot | Should be | Rendered |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `letterhead.name` | the candidate | the whole 380-char opening paragraph |\n| `date` | 16. August 2026 | a body paragraph containing \"0 % auf 90 %.\" |\n| `body` | 3–5 rich paragraphs | **empty** |\n| `salutation` / `signoff` | market pair | **absent** |\n| `signature_name` | the candidate | the opening paragraph, again |\n\nWith no salutation the parser never starts the body, so every paragraph fell into the pre-salutation branch and rendered as recipient lines: plain text, hard line breaks, no bold, no paragraph spacing.\n\n## The fix\n\n`complete_letter_text` synthesises the market salutation, sign-off and signature name for a body-only letter, inserted **after** any leading subject/date furniture. It is called once from `validate_and_normalize`, so PDF, both DOCX scanners and the live preview all inherit it — and **every letter already stored renders correctly with no regeneration**. Verified idempotent, so a full letter still round-trips byte-identically.\n\nAlso in scope, because the same cutover caused them:\n\n- **Market etiquette** — `<market_conventions>`, the subject line and an app-supplied date are back in the prompt; the market is resolved from the posting's location, so US postings get US Letter instead of A4.\n- **Bold** — the prompts ask for keyword emphasis again (letter *and* résumé draft); `sanitize_markdown` already preserves `**…**`.\n- **ATS/quality panel** — `top_requirements` now comes from the `analyze_job` stage rather than the request the tailor surface sends empty. That single change un-starves the requirement metric, stops the empty list freezing the keyword chips through a pick-non-empty merge, and makes `regenerate_section` validate against the same list the run used. The renderer's `meta` is seeded from the aggregate instead of fabricated, which also stops a non-null stub short-circuiting the answers assistant's own extraction.\n- **`humanize`** ran after validation with gates that never looked at keyword coverage; it now rejects a rewrite that drops coverage past the existing threshold.\n- **Company research** reaches the letter again, opt-in, through the *same* `AI_RESEARCH_BUCKET` rate/concurrency limiter and provider daily ceiling as the existing command — one named constant, one runtime bucket, guard held across the call.\n- Predicate hardening: a name is capped at 64 chars / 8 tokens, a date at 48 / 8; the letterhead name falls back to the contact profile before the letter's first line.\n\n## Guardrails\n\nEvery existing letter test fed a *complete* letter — the shape the **old** prompt produced. That is exactly why this survived. Added adversarial body-only fixtures carrying the three traps from the real incident (long opening paragraph, digits-and-period paragraph, a bold keyword) plus PDF text-layer and DOCX `document.xml` contract tests, **verified failing** against a neutered `complete_letter_text`. A prompt↔export lock test names the synthesiser that must be retired if the prompt ever stops delegating.\n\n## Verification\n\n`cargo test --lib` 4051 passed · `cargo test --test architecture` 18 · clippy `--all-features -D warnings` clean · `cargo fmt --check` clean · `pnpm test` 6898 passed / 478 files · typecheck 13/13 · `lint:strict --max-warnings 0` clean · `gen:ipc:check` in sync.\n\nSecurity review found no HIGH/CRITICAL. Its MEDIUM findings are fixed here: a third export path (`GenerationCard`) still sent no locale and would have appended an English salutation to a German letter — a defect this branch introduced — and the new fence assertions were vacuous until the hostile payload was extended to forge the tags it asserts on (mutation-tested red, then green).\n\n## Known gaps, recorded not fixed\n\nPipeline letters still lose link injection (TS-side, needs porting); tone/mode/applicant-preference conditioning is still absent from the staged letter prompt. The Jobs-page match badge is a cached score of the *saved default* résumé and no surface has ever re-scored it after a generation — making it move is a product decision, not a regression fix.\n\nADR-034 records the ownership split.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Generate market-aware résumés and cover letters using location, date, tone, and formatting conventions.\n  * Optionally research companies for more tailored cover letters, while generation continues if research is unavailable.\n  * Use resolved job requirements to improve drafting, validation, and humanization.\n  * Preview and export cover letters with consistent locale-specific salutations, sign-offs, signatures, and candidate-name fallbacks.\n  * Infer markets from job locations for more accurate previews and PDF/DOCX exports.\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved handling of blank names, dates, letter formatting, and export metadata.\n  * Reduced sensitive detail in research logs.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added cover-letter export behavior documentation.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-08-16T03:27:19Z","updated_at":"2026-08-16T03:48:11Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"987d0cdb001347d95d119c6bd3d288ce1c19eb4a","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":10964600421,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACjYqGZQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","color":"0075ca","default":true,"description":"Documentation and markdown"},{"id":11212541136,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHM0A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/app/extension","name":"app/extension","color":"1d76db","default":false,"description":"Changes to apps/extension"},{"id":11212541200,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHNEA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/app/desktop","name":"app/desktop","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Changes to apps/desktop"},{"id":11212541282,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHNYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/pkg/shared","name":"pkg/shared","color":"1abc9c","default":false,"description":"Changes to packages/shared"},{"id":11212541380,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHNxA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/pkg/prompts","name":"pkg/prompts","color":"2bbbad","default":false,"description":"Changes to packages/prompts"},{"id":11212541572,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHOhA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/rust","name":"rust","color":"dea584","default":false,"description":"Rust backend (apps/desktop/src-tauri)"},{"id":11212541661,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHO3Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/frontend","name":"frontend","color":"7057ff","default":false,"description":"React renderer (apps/desktop/src/renderer)"}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pulls/997/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pulls/997/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunt